  "notes": "USAGE:\n{駆除|くじょ} is used both as a noun and with する to form a verb. It applies primarily to pests and unwanted organisms, not to people or abstract concepts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {害虫|がいちゅう}{駆除|くじょ} (pest extermination)\n- ネズミの{駆除|くじょ} (rat extermination)\n- {駆除|くじょ}{業者|ぎょうしゃ} (extermination company)\n- {外来種|がいらいしゅ}を{駆除|くじょ}する (to eradicate invasive species)\n- {駆除|くじょ}{作業|さぎょう} (extermination work)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{退治|たいじ} also means to exterminate or get rid of pests, but has a broader, sometimes more dramatic connotation (e.g., {鬼退治|おにたいじ}, slaying demons). {駆除|くじょ} is more technical and practical.",
